# EtToggleSwitch Component

## Purpose & Scope

`EtToggleSwitch` is a controlled toggle switch component for the eToro design system. It provides a flexible, accessible switch with:

- **Two sizes**: small (~75% scale) and medium (default, native size, 100% scale)
- **Extends native Switch API**: familiar `value`/`onValueChange` pattern for easy migration
- **Native animations**: uses platform-native Switch animations
- **Haptic feedback**: enabled by default
- **Theme-aware colors**: automatically uses design system colors
- **Gesture handler integration**: uses `Switch` from `react-native-gesture-handler` for proper touch handling inside drawer navigators

**Does NOT handle:**

- Form validation logic (handle in parent)
- Label text (use external EtText or ListItem wrapper)
- Uncontrolled mode (always requires `value` + `onValueChange`)

## Entry Points & Contracts

### `EtToggleSwitch` (main component)

```tsx
<EtToggleSwitch
  value: boolean                    // required - controlled state
  onValueChange: (value: boolean) => void  // required - toggle callback
  size?: 'small' | 'medium'         // default: 'medium'
  disabled?: boolean                // default: false
  haptics?: boolean                 // default: true
  forceNativeSync?: boolean         // default: false - use in bottom sheets
  trackColor?: { false?: string; true?: string }  // optional overrides
  thumbColor?: string               // optional override
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
  testID?: string
  accessibilityLabel?: string
/>
```

### Types

| Type               | Values                  |
| ------------------ | ----------------------- |
| `ToggleSwitchSize` | `'small'` \| `'medium'` |

## Usage Patterns

### Basic usage

```tsx
const [on, setOn] = useState(false);
<EtToggleSwitch value={on} onValueChange={setOn} />;
```

### Medium size

```tsx
<EtToggleSwitch value={on} onValueChange={setOn} size="medium" />
```

### Disabled state

```tsx
<EtToggleSwitch value={on} onValueChange={setOn} disabled />
```

### Custom colors (optional - uses theme by default)

```tsx
<EtToggleSwitch value={on} onValueChange={setOn} trackColor={{ true: '#0eb12e', false: '#ccc' }} thumbColor="#fff" />
```

### In a settings list

```tsx
<ListItem
  title="Push Notifications"
  subtitle="Receive alerts for price movements"
  right={<EtToggleSwitch value={notifications} onValueChange={setNotifications} />}
/>
```

### Inside bottom sheets (iOS fix)

```tsx
// When using EtToggleSwitch inside @gorhom/bottom-sheet,
// enable forceNativeSync to fix iOS native Switch visual sync issues
const [isAdvancedView, setIsAdvancedView] = useState(false);
<EtToggleSwitch value={isAdvancedView} onValueChange={setIsAdvancedView} forceNativeSync />;
```

## Anti-patterns

### ❌ Using without controlled state

```tsx
// BAD - no state management
<EtToggleSwitch onValueChange={handleChange} />
```

**Fix:** Always provide `value` prop with controlled state:

```tsx
const [on, setOn] = useState(false);
<EtToggleSwitch value={on} onValueChange={setOn} />;
```

### ❌ Using old EtToggle props

```tsx
// BAD - old API
<EtToggleSwitch trackColorOn="#green" trackColorOff="#gray" thumbColorDisabled="#999" />
```

**Fix:** Use native Switch prop format with valid hex or named colors:

```tsx
<EtToggleSwitch value={on} onValueChange={setOn} trackColor={{ true: '#0eb12e', false: '#cccccc' }} thumbColor="#ffffff" />
```

### ❌ Adding inline labels

```tsx
// BAD - component doesn't support labels
<EtToggleSwitch>Enable notifications</EtToggleSwitch>
```

**Fix:** Use external text or list item wrapper:

```tsx
<View style={styles.row}>
  <EtText>Enable notifications</EtText>
  <EtToggleSwitch value={on} onValueChange={setOn} />
</View>
```

## Dependencies & Edges

### Internal Dependencies

- `useEtoroTheme` - provides theme colors for styling
- Hooks:
  - `useToggleSwitchConfig` - derives colors from props and theme

### External Dependencies

- `expo-haptics` - haptic feedback on press
- `react-native-gesture-handler` - `Switch` component (used instead of `react-native` Switch for proper gesture coordination with drawer navigators)

### Design System Integration

- Colors come from theme (`useEtoroTheme().colors`):
  - Track On: `actionBrandText` (brand green)
  - Track Off: `bgGreyPrimary` (gray)
  - Track Disabled: `bgActionDisabled`
  - Thumb: white (`#ffffff`)
  - Thumb Disabled: `#bfbfbf`
- Sizes use scale transforms on native Switch (~51x31 iOS):
  - Small: 75% scale
  - Medium: 100% scale (native size, default)

## Patterns & Pitfalls

### Controlled Component Pattern

The switch is always controlled - parent owns state via `value` + `onValueChange`:

- `value` determines visual state
- `onValueChange` receives toggled boolean
- By default, never stores internal state (except when `forceNativeSync` is enabled)

### iOS Bottom Sheet Compatibility

When using EtToggleSwitch inside `@gorhom/bottom-sheet`, the native iOS Switch may not visually update when the value prop changes programmatically. This is a known React Native iOS bug ([#31975](https://github.com/facebook/react-native/issues/31975), [#50026](https://github.com/facebook/react-native/issues/50026)).

**Solution:** Enable `forceNativeSync` prop:

```tsx
<EtToggleSwitch value={on} onValueChange={setOn} forceNativeSync />
```

This enables internal state management that keeps the native Switch in sync while preserving smooth animations.

### Android Drawer Navigator Compatibility

On Android, the native `Switch` from `react-native` doesn't coordinate properly with `react-native-gesture-handler` used by drawer navigators (React Navigation/Expo Router). This causes touches to be intercepted by the drawer's gesture handler instead of reaching the Switch.

**Solution:** The component uses `Switch` from `react-native-gesture-handler` instead of the native `react-native` Switch. This ensures proper gesture coordination with drawer navigators on Android - no additional props or wrappers needed.

### Extends Native SwitchProps

For easy migration from native Switch or existing EtToggle:

- Same `value`/`onValueChange` signature
- Same `trackColor`/`thumbColor` prop format
- Added `size` and `haptics` as eToro-specific enhancements

### Animation Behavior

Uses the platform-native Switch animations for consistent, performant behavior on iOS and Android.

### Accessibility

Built-in accessibility support via native Switch:

- Native Switch provides `switch` accessibility role automatically
- `accessibilityLabel` prop for custom screen reader text (defaults to "Toggle switch on/off")
- Native Switch handles `disabled` state accessibility

